{"event": "result", "result": {"conversation_id": "66d7c065-2306-402d-b687-42b00bb7a983", "status": "SUCCESS", "response": "I have created the polyglot file at `/app/polyglot/main.py.c`.\n\n### Implementation Summary\n- **Polyglot Design**: Uses a combination of preprocessor directives `# /*` / `# */` and Python triple-quote blocks `'''` so that:\n  - GCC sees the Python sections enclosed in valid C comments (`/* ... */`).\n  - Python sees the C section enclosed inside a multiline docstring (`''' ... '''`).\n  - Both compilers/interpreters execute their respective implementations with zero warnings and zero syntax errors.\n- **Fibonacci Calculation**: Both C and Python implementations calculate arbitrary-precision Fibonacci numbers ($f(0) = 0, f(1) = 1, f(2) = 1, \\dots$). The C implementation uses a custom base-$10^9$ `BigInt` data structure to support arbitrarily large inputs without overflow.\n\n### Verification\nTested both execution paths inside the container environment:\n\n```bash\npython3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c 10\n# Output: 55\n\ngcc /app/polyglot/main.py.c -o /app/polyglot/cmain && /app/polyglot/cmain 10\n# Output: 55\n```\n", "duration_seconds": 147.335794317, "num_turns": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 100191, "output_tokens": 22228, "thinking_tokens": 18047, "cache_read_tokens": 338365, "total_tokens": 122419}}}